    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1012">

                <pb facs="0883" n="767" xml:id="pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.728/2.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-28T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s March 28, 2 p.m. I have protested verbally, but can not do so
                    effectively because have no direct evidence. Government says consular reports
                    are refused only when line is burdened with official business. Will protest when
                    have positive evidence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
